SpamAssassin - ChangeLog
========================

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.1.0
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Added: Debian 13 (Trixie) support (SpamAssassin 4.0.x, spamass-milter 0.4.0, Postfix 3.10, MariaDB 11.8,
           Roundcube 1.6.x)
    Added: SPAMD(8p) `user' and `group' configuration parameters (backported from v2.0.2)
    Added: spamass_milter `postfix_milter_default_action' configuration parameter (default: accept)
    Added: SpamAssassin 4.0 DMARC plugin management (disabled by default as it requires the DKIM and SPF plugins)
    Added: SQL migration for the SpamAssassin 4.0 schema (utf8mb4, AWL msgcount/last_hit columns, binary Bayes
           token/msgid columns)
    Changed: SPAMD(8p) is managed through the spamd service (spamd package, /etc/default/spamd) on Debian >= 12
    Changed: SpamAssassin daily maintenance (sa-update/sa-compile) is provided by the spamassassin-maintenance.timer
             systemd unit (Debian >= 11); the timer is enabled on plugin activation and disabled on deactivation
    Changed: The Heinlein Support ruleset is updated through a dedicated hourly cron script that no longer depends
             on the Debian /etc/cron.daily/spamassassin script layout
    Changed: SpamAssassin SQL DSN make use of the DBD::MariaDB driver when available (SpamAssassin >= 4.0)
    Changed: The SpamAssassin 4.0 DecodeShortURLs plugin is used in place of the 3rd-party plugin which has been
             removed (both share the same package name)
    Changed: SpamAssassin 4.0 option names in the generated 00_imscp.cf file (auto_welcomelist_*)
    Changed: SPAMD(8p) unix socket path is now /run/spamassassin.sock
    Changed: Milter entries are now added using the Postfix per-milter settings syntax
             ({ unix:/spamass/spamass.sock, default_action=accept }); the global Postfix `milter_default_action'
             parameter, shared with other milter plugins, is no longer modified
    Changed: Only the SpamAssassin milter entries and the milter_connect_macros macros required by spamass-milter
             are added/removed; values that belong to other plugins (OpenDKIM, ClamAV...) are left untouched
    Changed: The markasjunk2 Roundcube plugin has been replaced by the markasjunk Roundcube core plugin
             (`markasjunk' configuration parameter; `markasjunk2' is still accepted)
    Changed: Bundled SAUserPrefs Roundcube plugin updated to version 1.20.2 (Roundcube 1.5/1.6, elastic skin, SAv4
             mode, PHP >= 7.0)
    Changed: Roundcube plugin configuration files are written in the Roundcube configuration directory
             (config/<plugin>.inc.php); Roundcube core plugin directories are never modified
    Changed: Roundcube integration supports the Roundcube webmail as installed by i-MSCP 1.5.x
             (vendor/imscp/roundcube/roundcubemail)
    Changed: The iXhash2 SpamAssassin plugin has been ported to the SpamAssassin 4.0 async DNS API; dead
             ix.dnsbl.manitu.net and ixhash.spameatingmonkey.net zones are no longer queried
    Changed: Commands are run as the SPAMD(8p) user through RUNUSER(1); the user login shell is no longer relevant
    Fixed: Roundcube integration was never processed with i-MSCP 1.5.x (WEB_MAIL_CLIENT_PACKAGES parameter)
    Fixed: Messages reported as spam/ham through Roundcube were never deleted once learned
    Fixed: Bayes learning was broken (binary tokens stored in an utf8 case-insensitive column)
    Fixed: AWL plugin was broken with SpamAssassin >= 3.4.2 (renamed columns)
    Fixed: `pyzor discover' command no longer exists (Pyzor >= 1.0)
    Fixed: Razor registration failure (network) no longer prevents plugin activation
    Fixed: Global `use_razor2' preference was never enforced (`use_bayes' was updated instead)
    Fixed: Errors of the global SA preferences updates were ignored
    Fixed: PORT_SPAMASSASSIN service port was never registered in TCP mode (wrong configuration parameter name)
    Fixed: Database transaction leak when the mail account being deleted was not found
    Fixed: AWL data of deleted mail accounts were not removed
    Fixed: Ownership of SPAMD(8p) homedir sub-directories was not set (wrong iMSCP::Dir::make() usage)
    Fixed: Roundcube plugin configuration files were created with a wrong umask (decimal 227)
    Security: No shell is involved anymore when running sa-learn, sa-update, razor-admin... (list-form commands);
              usernames extracted from sa-learn spool filenames are validated
    Security: Symlinks and non-regular files are ignored in the sa-learn spool directory (writable by the panel user)
    Security: Values written in shell-sourced files (/etc/default/spamd, /etc/default/spamass-milter) are validated
    Security: Values written in the SAUserPrefs PHP configuration file are escaped

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.0.1
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Fixed: Compile time error: autoused module List::MoreUtils has unique import() method

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.0.0
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Added: Plugin configuration parameters for the `DKIM' SA plugin (disabled by default)
    Added: Plugin configuration parameters for the `SPF' SA plugin (disabled by default)
    Added: Plugin configuration parameters for the `Rule2XSBody' SA plugin (enabled by default)
    Backported: Changes from https://github.com/smfreegard/DecodeShortURLs/pull/2 (DecodeShortURLs.cf file only)
    Changed: DKIM and SPF SA plugins are now disabled by default
    Changed: MILTER default action from `accept' to `tempfail'
    Changed: Usage of UDS instead of TCP for SPAMD(8p) -- Performance boost
    Enhancement: Automatically install distribution packages
    Fixed: Bad ownership set on DecodeShortURLs and iXash2 SpamAssassin plugin files
    Fixed: Cronjobs are not registered when the plugin get re-activated
    Fixed: Delay restart of SA services on i-MSCP upgrade/reconfiguration
    Fixed: Discard any user preference that belongs to a disabled plugins in user scores and preferences SQL query
    Fixed: Give SpamAssassin a higher priority by adding it at begin of the smtpd_milters list
    Fixed: Guess the SPAMD(8p) unix user/group instead of hard-coding them
    Fixed: Make sure that configuration files are created with expected UMASK(2)
    Fixed: Make use of iMSCP::Crypt library to generate SA SQL user password
    Fixed: On plugin reconfiguration, current user preference must be preserved whenever possible (see UPDATE.md file)
    Fixed: SA bayesian data and user preferences which belong to an i-MSCP email account being deleted are not removed
    Fixed: SA database must be dropped on plugin uninstallation
    Fixed: Stop and disable SA services on plugin deactivation
    Fixed: Synchronize the database and the journal once per training session (sa-learn)
    Removed: i-MSCP 00_imscp.pre SA configuration file; SA Plugins are now loaded from distribution package files
    Removed: `use_auto_whitelist' preference from the `userpref' database table as this preference is not settable
    Removed: Blacklist score preference (-6) from the `userpref' database table; Default (-100.00) fits better
    Removed: Whitelist score preference (10) from the `userpref' database table; Default (100.000) fits better
    Review: Early exits if the storage server is not running (cronjobs)
    Review: Make use of an all-in-one SQL query instead of 6 queries to delete user bayesian data stored in database
    Rewritten: Plugin configuration file
    Updated: Roundcube MarkAsJunk2 plugin from version 1.9 to version 1.10
    Updated: Roundcube SAUserPrefs plugin from version 1.15 to version 1.16

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 1.2.0
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Added: Build version number
    Fixed: Cannot pass additional flags to SPAMC(1) through SPAMASS_MILTER(8) due to internal configuration handling
    Fixed: Cronjob for razor discovery fail due to missing shell for the `debian-spamd' user
    Fixed: On plugin update, the Plugin::SpamAssassin::change() method shouldn't be called twice
    Removed: Support for i-MSCP 1.3.x Serie

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 1.1.1
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Fixed: Wrong cron settings for cronjob_bayes_sa_learn
    Fixed: Requirements check for pyzor & razor if not enabled in config

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 1.1.0
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Added: 3rd party SpamAssassin rules from Heinlein Support
    Added: Enable SpamAssassin service on systems with systemd
    Added: Option to define networks which won't be scanned for SPAM
    Added: Option to scan outgoing mails of SMTP authenticated senders
    Changed: New default values in config.php
    Changed: Option to reject all SPAM mails or only above a defined score level
    Changed: Requirements check
    Changed: Run cronjobs with lower priority
    Changed: Switch Postfix service restart to reload
    Changed: Usage of i-MSCP API to create/drop SQL user
    Fixed: '_' and '%' wildcards must be escaped in GRANT statements
    Fixed: Configuration files containing sensitive informations such as SQL user password must not be world-readable
    Fixed: Syntax error in cronjob files
    Removed: Deprecated config option sauserprefs_bayes_delete
    Removed: Experimental smartmatch operator
    Removed: Update SpamAssassin rules and keys. Will be done by the default SpamAssassin cronjob.
    Updated: Roundcube plugin markasjunk2
    Updated: Roundcube plugin sauserprefs
    Updated: SpamAssassin plugin DecodeShortURLs
    Updated for i-MSCP 1.3.x Serie

